The '''2026 Pennsylvania House of Representatives election''' will be held on November 3, 2026, alongside the other [[2026 United States elections]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Booker |first=Brakkton |date=July 29, 2025 |title=The 2026 midterms are officially underway |url=https://www.politico.com/newsletters/the-recast/2025/07/29/2026-elections-battleground-senate-candidates-00481526 |access-date=August 7, 2025 |website=Politico}}</ref> Voters will elect members of the [[Pennsylvania House of Representatives]] in all 203 of the [[U.S. state]] of [[Pennsylvania]]'s legislative districts to serve a two-year term.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pennsylvania House of Representatives elections, 2026 |url=https://ballotpedia.org/Pennsylvania_House_of_Representatives_elections,_2026 |access-date=August 10, 2025 |website=Ballotpedia}}</ref>

==Special elections==
===22nd district===
After being elected [[Lehigh County, Pennsylvania|Lehigh County]] Executive, Representative [[Joshua Siegel (politician)|Joshua Siegel]] resigned from the state House on December 17, 2025. A special election is scheduled for February 24.<ref name="specials">{{cite news |title=Josh Siegel resigns from Pa. House to become Lehigh County executive. Here's when the election will be to replace him |url=https://www.mcall.com/2025/12/17/siegel-special-election-pa-house/ |access-date=December 18, 2025 |work=The Morning Call |date=December 17, 2025}}</ref> The Democratic Party initially chose Julian Guridy, a staffer to state Senator [[Nick Miller (politician)|Nick Miller]], as its candidate. However, Guridy did not met the residency requirement to run for the state House and was forced to withdraw.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Addy |first1=Jason |title=Pa. residency rule forced Julian Guridy's exit from Lehigh Valley special election |url=https://www.lehighvalleynews.com/elections/pa-residency-rule-forced-julian-guridys-exit-from-lehigh-valley-special-election |access-date=January 14, 2026 |work=Lehigh Valley News |date=January 12, 2026}}</ref> He was replaced by [[Allentown School District|Allentown School Board]] member Ana Tiburcio.<ref>{{cite news |title=Democrats choose new Pa. House candidate in Lehigh County race as Julian Guridy drops out 'for personal reasons' |url=https://www.mcall.com/2026/01/10/allentown-state-house-special-election-democrats/ |access-date=January 12, 2026 |work=The Morning Call |date=January 11, 2026}}</ref> The Republican Party has selected its [[2022 Pennsylvania House of Representatives election|2022]] nominee Robert E. Smith Jr., a former Allentown School Board member.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Orenstein |first1=Robert H. |last2=Reinhard |first2=Katherine |title=Julian Guridy and Robert E. Smith Jr. selected for 22nd state House District special election |url=https://armchairlehighvalley.substack.com/p/julian-guridy-and-robert-e-smith |access-date=January 5, 2026 |work=Armchair Lehigh Valley |date=January 4, 2026}}</ref> Tiburcio won the election.

