===42nd district===
Representative [[Dan Miller (Pennsylvania politician)|Dan Miller]] was elected as a judge in [[Allegheny County, Pennsylvania|Allegheny County]] in 2025 and resigned from the state House on December 17, 2025. A special election is scheduled for February 24.<ref name="specials" /> The Democratic Party selected [[Dormont, Pennsylvania|Dormont]] borough councilor [[Jennifer Mazzocco]]. The Republican Party selected [[2024 Pennsylvania House of Representatives election|2024]] nominee Joseph Leckenby.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Potter |first1=Chris |title=Democrat Mazzocco to face GOP's Leckenby in state House race to replace Dan Miller |url=https://www.wesa.fm/politics-government/2026-01-03/democrat-mazzocco-republican-leckenby-dan-miller-pennsylvania-house |access-date=January 5, 2026 |publisher=90.5 WESA |date=January 3, 2026}}</ref> Mazzocco won the election.

