===79th district===
Representative [[Louis Schmitt Jr.|Lou Schmitt]] was elected as a judge in [[Blair County, Pennsylvania|Blair County]] in 2025 and resigned on December 31.<ref name="Ecker&Schmitt" /> A special election is scheduled for March 17.<ref name="Mar17">{{cite news |last1=Northup |first1=Alton |title=Pennsylvania House speaker sets 2 more special elections after resignations |url=https://www.yourerie.com/news/pennsylvania-house-speaker-sets-2-more-special-elections-after-resignations/?nxsparam=6 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |work=YourErie.com |date=January 2, 2026}}</ref> The Republican Party chose Andrea Verobish, a staffer for Congressman [[Glenn Thompson (politician)|Glenn Thompson]], as its candidate.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ulrich |first1=Steve |title=HD-79: Verobish Selected as GOP Candidate In Special Election To Replace Schmitt |url=https://www.politicspa.com/hd-79-verobish-selected-as-gop-candidate-in-special-election-to-replace-schmitt/145437/ |access-date=January 17, 2026 |work=PoliticsPA |date=January 16, 2026}}</ref> The Democratic Party nominated registered nurse Caleb McCoy.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kibler |first1=William |title=Blair County Democrats tab newcomer for special election to fill 79th District seat McCoy launches bid for Schmitt's former seat in state House |url=https://www.altoonamirror.com/news/local-news/2026/01/pa-house-79th-special-election-democrats-nominate-mccoy-newcomer/ |access-date=January 24, 2026 |work=Altoona Mirror |date=January 24, 2026}}</ref> Verobish won the election.

