===193rd district===
Representative [[Torren Ecker]] was elected as a judge in [[Adams County, Pennsylvania|Adams County]] in 2025 and resigned on December 30.<ref name="Ecker&Schmitt">{{cite news |last1=Scicchitano |first1=Eric |title=Special elections set for Pa. House, results won't likely change power dynamic |url=https://www.alliednews.com/cnhi_network/special-elections-set-for-pa-house-results-won-t-likely-change-power-dynamic/article_00ee8225-5f0a-5b31-8640-51fbd82b0116.html |access-date=January 24, 2026 |work=Allied News |date=January 2, 2026}}</ref> A special election is scheduled for March 17.<ref name="Mar17" /> On January 15, Republicans in Cumberland and Adams counties selected Ecker staffer [[Catherine Wallen]] to be their nominee.<ref name="f439">{{cite web | last=Cooper-White | first=Michael | title=Wallen chosen Republican candidate for 193rd seat in special election | website=Gettysburg Times | date=October 31, 2025 | url=https://www.gettysburgtimes.com/news/local/article_8cf00420-5131-4137-a670-47403536713a.html | access-date=January 17, 2026}}</ref> On January 24, Democrats nominated former [[Harrisburg Area Community College]] official Todd Crawley.<ref name="v562">{{cite web | last=Sherry | first=Hayden | title=Democratic nominee chosen for State House special election in Cumberland, Adams counties | publisher=ABC27 | date=January 24, 2026 | url=https://www.abc27.com/news/democratic-nominee-chosen-for-state-house-special-election-in-cumberland-adams-counties/| access-date=January 24, 2026}}</ref> Wallen won the election.

