===196th district===
Representative [[Seth Grove]] announced that he would resign effective January 31. He had previously stated that he would not seek reelection in 2026. Since January 1, Grove was CEO of the Pennsylvania Aggregates and Concrete Association, a lobbying group. Because he was also the minority chair of the Labor & Industry Committee, Grove faced accusations of a conflict of interest and announced his resignation under scrutiny.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Owens |first1=Dennis |last2=Stockburger |first2=George |title=Pennsylvania lawmaker resigns amid conflict of interest complaints |url=https://www.abc27.com/pennsylvania-politics/pennsylvania-lawmaker-resigns-amid-conflict-of-interest-complaints/ |access-date=January 29, 2026 |publisher=ABC27 |date=January 29, 2026}}</ref> A special election coincided with the primary election on May 19.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thompson |first1=Ian |title=Special election called to fill York County state house seat |url=https://www.fox43.com/article/news/special-election-called-to-fill-york-county-state-house-seat/521-0b55f892-ea41-4565-ab45-79acce2c3388 |access-date=February 3, 2026 |publisher=FOX43 |date=February 2, 2026}}</ref> The Democratic Party nominated [[West Manchester Township, Pennsylvania|West Manchester Township]] supervisor and former gubernatorial press secretary Ron Ruman. The Republican Party nominated attorney [[George Margetas]] who won.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Doran |first1=Brady |title=Democratic candidate announces nomination in PA 196th special election |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/democratic-candidate-announces-nomination-pa-144710912.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAEf6CwwbEjoIh3MWJZZxWZnaj8u4PWzTA7u0i86UvE21bQVRbHMgPZePDFPqiAaLp8qO0FYntfQ76az-7VSY0bwHOIz3VNgSCwpDKWvHr0-ASruSPEkw-n5SA7ZFe_sfcqhlRyy8nBQ6sJqcwAGRwQy-CTltKT6aP1au0t2yKiYO |access-date=April 28, 2026 |via=Yahoo! News |publisher=WHTM |date=March 26, 2026}}</ref>

