===12th district===
Representative [[Stephenie Scialabba]] previously announced plans to retire at the conclusion of the current term.<ref name="pplist" /> She later announced her resignation effective March 31.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ulrich |first1=Steve |title=Scialabba Announces Resignation From Butler County PA House Seat |url=https://www.politicspa.com/scialabba-announces-resignation-from-butler-county-pa-house-seat/145941/ |access-date=March 25, 2026 |work=PoliticsPA |date=March 24, 2026}}</ref> A special election took place August 18.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Riese |first1=Tom |title=Butler County special election for Scialabba's House seat set for August |url=https://www.wesa.fm/politics-government/2026-04-08/house-district-special-election-butler-scialabba |access-date=April 10, 2026 |publisher=90.5 WESA |date=April 8, 2026}}</ref> Scott Timko was the Republican candidate. [[Brandon Dukes]] was the Democratic candidate.<ref>{{cite news |last1=White |first1=Bella |title=Bureau of Elections ready to mail out ballots later this month ahead of special election |url=https://www.butlereagle.com/20260708/bureau-of-elections-confirms-mail-in-ballots-ahead-of-special-election/ |access-date=July 11, 2026 |work=Butler Eagle |date=July 8, 2026}}</ref> Dukes won by less than 100 votes,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Stanton |first1=Emma |title=Democrat Brandon Dukes wins House seat in Butler by less than 100 votes over Republican Scott Timko |url=https://triblive.com/local/regional/brandon-dukes-wins-house-seat-in-butler-by-less-than-100-votes/ |access-date=19 August 2026 |work=TribLive |date=August 19, 2026}}</ref> becoming the first Democrat to represent this district since [[Patricia Carone]] switched parties in the 1990s.<ref>https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2026/08/special-election-upset-pennsylvania-house-butler-county-democrats-elections/</ref> With the win, the Democrats increased their majority in the Pennsylvania House to 103-100.<ref>{{cite news |title=Dukes Win Expands Democrats’ Pennsylvania House Majority |url=https://www.mychesco.com/a/news/government/dukes-win-expands-democrats-pennsylvania-house-majority/ |access-date=October 6, 2026 |publisher=My Cheso |date=August 22, 2026}}</ref>

